      <section class="problem-section">
        <h2>Safe Beaches for Kids</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Paje:</strong> Lagoon swimming safe at high tide; gentle waves; watch for sea urchins at low tide; camel rides at sunset</li>
          <li><strong>Jambiani:</strong> Safe swimming; tides expose seaweed farms — watch your step; cultural village visits available</li>
          <li><strong>Bwejuu:</strong> Palm-fringed, relaxed, family-friendly, no tide issues; wide beach for running</li>
          <li><strong>Kiwengwa:</strong> Protected lagoon, all-inclusive resorts, shallow water for children</li>
          <li><strong>Stone Town / Forodhani:</strong> Day visit only; night market requires supervision; uneven surfaces</li>
        </ul>

      <section class="problem-section">
        <h2>Kid-Approved Activities</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Mnemba snorkeling:</strong> Pristine coral, green sea turtles, colorful fish — 2-hour trip, minimum age 5</li>
          <li><strong>Dolphin watching:</strong> Kizimkazi morning trips; pods surfing waves; 3-hour excursion</li>
          <li><strong>Beach horseback riding:</strong> Sunset or morning rides; suitable for beginners & children 8+</li>
          <li><strong>Cultural village visits:</strong> Jambiani or Kizimbani; seaweed farming, traditional crafts, Swahili cooking</li>
          <li><strong>Stone Town walking tour:</strong> House of Wonders, Palace Museum, Freddie Mercury House — uneven surfaces, bring water</li>
          <li><strong>Prison Island + Nakupenda:</strong> Giant tortoises (100+ years), snorkeling; 2-hour boat trip from Stone Town</li>
        </ul>

      <section class="problem-section">
        <h2>Family-Friendly Accommodations Comparison</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Resorts with kids' clubs:</strong> Essque Zalu Zanzibar, Riu Palace Zanzibar, Riu Jambo — supervised activities, children's menus</li>
          <li><strong>Boutique hotels:</strong> Zuri Zanzibar, Nungwi Dreams by Mantis — personalized service, family rooms available</li>
          <li><strong>Beach bungalows:</strong> Kiwengwa Beach Bungalows, Paje Bungalows — self-catering, more space</li>
          <li><strong>Dhow Coast recommendation:</n> Mix of resort + bungalow for variety; all properties offer cribs on request</li>
        </ul>

      <section class="problem-section">
        <h2>What to Pack for Zanzibar with Kids</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>High-SPF sunscreen (reef-safe, SPF 50+)</li>
          <li>UV-protective swim shirts (rash guards)</li>
          <li>Water shoes / sea urchin guards</li>
          <li> hat with chin strap (windy coast)</li>
          <li>Child carrier for stone town walking</li>
          <li>Basic first aid: plasters, antiseptic, oral rehydration salts</li>
        </ul>

